{"id":242462934570436,"type":"album","name":"Kollaps","artist":"Einstürzende Neubauten","year":1981,"weight":20,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710908.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-cd457818-f2ed-4668-bd8f-4262fe015fee/mbid-cd457818-f2ed-4668-bd8f-4262fe015fee-23428871208.png","kind":"Album","tracks":14,"country":"DE","yt":"wTIOkvLfEF4","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/einsturzende-neubauten/kollaps-3"},"desc":"Kollaps is the first official LP by Einstürzende Neubauten, released in 1981 on German label ZickZack as #ZZ 65. The songs are a mixture of rough punk tunes as well as industrial noises obtained from self-made music machines, electronics, and found objects such as metal plates. The album was reissued in 2002 with Stahldubversions , originally released in 1982. Blixa Bargeld, N.U. Unruh and F.M. Einheit appear on the album. Jet'M is a cover of the Serge Gainsbourg song Je t'aime moi non plus . Trouser Press described Kollaps as \"one of the most shocking visions ever committed to vinyl.\" ."},"artist_ref":{"id":83484579097567,"name":"Einsturzende Neubauten","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Neubauten.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":274994627985231,"type":"genre","name":"Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":604,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"}],"lists":[{"id":27176113490870,"name":"RYM Top — Experimental — Industrial","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":56,"year":null,"note":null,"total":79,"scaruffi":null},{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":389,"year":null,"note":null,"total":877,"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","src":"charts","grp":"1001 Albums","list_year":null,"rank":476,"year":1981,"note":null,"total":999,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[],"book_tracks":[{"id":242462934570436,"artist":"Einstürzende Neubauten","artist_id":83484579097567,"ti